  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#images\n\n> If image's media data has no intrinsic dimensions (e.g. it's a vector graphic with no specified content size), then return a promise rejected with an InvalidStateError exception and abort these steps.\n\nCould we clarify that a vector graphic with an explicit zero size would be treated as having no intrinsic dimensions?\n\nExample:\n\n``` svg\n<svg width=\"0\" height=\"0\" viewBox=\"0 0 1 1\">\n```\n\n(or just one of them being zero)\n\nFwiw, the case is a bit similar to the ImageData constructor that says:\n\n> If both sw and sh are non-zero, return the new ImageData object. If one or both of sw and sh are zero, then the constructor must throw an IndexSizeError exception instead.\n",
